# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Hongwei Du et al. (2025). Universal Machine Learning Interatomic Potentials are Ready for Solid Ion Conductors.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2502.09970  arXiv:2502.09970v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2502.09970v1 (sha256 35f5dddce92c8881...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 230 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/du2025.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the six pretrained universal MLIPs evaluated (MatterSim,
# MACE, SevenNet, ORB, CHGNet, M3GNet; checkpoints not identified), their
# energy and force MAEs on the non-equilibrium halide-electrolyte test
# data stated in Sec. 3.2, and the DFT-labelled SSE data set built for the
# benchmark. Errors per sulfide/oxide system, near-equilibrium ranges,
# formation-energy, hull-energy, elastic-moduli and diffusivity benchmarks
# are shown in figures or given as ranges and are not encoded; the
# MatterSim application studies of Li3YCl6 and Li6PS5Cl are not encoded.

