###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The model versions (checkpoints) are not identified in the version read, so none is linked to a registry model. MatterSim applies the registry method M3GNet and SevenNet applies NequIP, as in the registry convention; ORBFF is recorded under ORB.
# - The halide test snapshots are said to come from heated DeePMD trajectories, while the benchmark data set is described as AIMD/DeepGen snapshots labelled with DFT; the relation between the two is not explicit.
# - Formation-energy, E_above_hull, bulk and shear moduli and Li-ion diffusivity errors are in figures (Figs. 8-10, S16-S33); near-equilibrium errors are given only as ranges over models.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/du2025.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

